    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469-a2">

                <pb facs="0480" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg468"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Klieforth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Czechoslovak Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clementis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Praha</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-03">July 3, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of June 30, 1945 informing me of the unfortunate and
                    regrettable incident on June 24th at Česky Krumlov–Prachatice, of which the
                    Czechoslovak Vice-Premier, His Excellency, Viliam Široky, was a victim.</p>
                <p>Immediately upon the receipt of your note I applied to the Vice Premier for an
                    appointment which he granted for 11 o’clock a.m. this morning, and accompanied
                    by Lt. Col. Woldike, the Military Attaché of the Embassy, I extended to him in
                    the name of my Government my deep regrets and apologies, which he was good
                    enough to accept. At the same time I assured him that the U.S. Army authorities
                    have been asked to take the necessary steps appropriate under the
                    circumstances.</p>
                <p>A copy of your note under acknowledgment with reference to the other matters
                    raised in it was transmitted to the officer commanding the U.S. Army unit
                    referred to for his information and such action as is necessary and appropriate
                    under the circumstances.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
